package fcp:connector@1.0.0;

/// The host-facing component contract for an FCP connector.
///
/// Each request and response is one canonical CBOR value, without a schema
/// prefix, JSON envelope, or length prefix. The method selects the existing FCP
/// request/response type. `configure` accepts the connector configuration object
/// and returns its configuration result; `handshake` maps HandshakeRequest to
/// HandshakeResponse; `health` accepts an empty map and returns HealthSnapshot;
/// `invoke` maps InvokeRequest to InvokeResponse. Business failures are ordinary
/// InvokeResponse values with an error status, not traps or a second envelope.
/// Unknown methods and structural protocol failures must fail the call.
///
/// The host retains one instance through configuration, handshake, health and
/// invocation. Capability tokens name the actual instance reported by health.
/// Instances are scoped to an exact zone and operation with immutable sandbox
/// policy. A failed, timed-out or cancelled dispatch retires the instance; the
/// host must not silently recreate it and replay a request with old authority.
///
/// Request and response bodies are capped at 16 MiB, with a possibly smaller
/// response limit chosen by the host. The sandbox also bounds guest memory,
/// execution fuel and wall time. The CBOR recipient rejects trailing bytes,
/// noncanonical encodings and responses with mismatched request identities.
world connector {
    export fcp-dispatch: func(method: string, request: list<u8>) -> list<u8>;
}
